[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1082","stub":{"id":"1082","section":"4. NC Route 9 below Lake Adger Dam to Big Level Road","altname":"","river":"Green","difficulty":"ItoII","states":["USA-NCR"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"341","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"","id":"109657","location":{"latitude":"35.333458","longitude":"-82.184832"},"name":"Put in on river left.","distance":"0.01","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"put-in","description":"This is undeveloped county property. Gravel driveway may require AWD.","id":"4sInAbzNaSruu5zacvvlW","location":{"latitude":"35.333672","longitude":"-82.184599"},"name":"Parking for put in.","distance":"0.07","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"access","description":"","id":"N3ANoZWerWvxGjoattVjp","location":{"latitude":"35.332581","longitude":"-82.153424"},"name":"Parking for alternative access point ","distance":"3.12","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"access","description":"Parking is on the ROW, avoid blocking any driveways.","id":"h1MnzUPtgR76NHDk8qZdC","location":{"latitude":"35.337874","longitude":"-82.111047"},"name":"Parking for Big Level Rd takeout","distance":"7.17","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"other","description":"Take out on river right. Not a developed trail.","id":"114909","location":{"latitude":"35.337915","longitude":"-82.111317"},"name":"Take Out at Big Level Rd","distance":"7.17","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[],"detail":{"id":"1082","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"The 7 miles below Lake Adger Dam is a dam controlled run with beginner friendly rapids, deep pools and long boiling eddy lines. The dam generates power primarily in the afternoon and evening. Releases can be substantial, 500 to 1000 cfs, resulting in deep fast flows. There is not a posted release schedule or data online.  There is a gauge 45 miles downstream on the Broad (Boiling Springs). It takes about 15 hrs for the flow to reach the gauge, so you can see what the flow was the day before. Most releases start at 4 or 5 PM. There is usually no releases on weekends.\n\nA 3 mile float from the dam to Wilson Hill Road includes fast moving water, shoals, some play waves and strong eddies. The streambed is wide but do watch for strainers. The 4 miles from Wilson Hill to Big Level Road is slower but still worth the time. There are several strong eddy lines to play in and a couple of fun splat rocks. The scenary is primarily woodlands and there are several large rocks for breaks. Avoid island channels that are not obviously open. The exit of at least one channel was blocked by wood as of June 2022.\n\nAccess\n\nThere is a small parking lot below the bridge on Hwy 9 on river left. The driveway into the lot is steep. Check out the river left and right eddies for stern squirts.\n\nIf taking out at Wilson Hill Road, scout out parking and river egress prior to your trip.\n\nIf taking out at Big Level Road, there is a small goat path just before the bridge on river right. There may be a partially submerged rock at the base of the path. Park with caution on the right of ways adjacent to Big Level Road. Do not block driveways or gates.\n\nCredits\n\nRisa Callaway","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"7.2","correlations":[{"reachID":"1082","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"800","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"2000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"BROAD RIVER NEAR BOILING SPRINGS, NC","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"02151500","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"341","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"1.54","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"35.21126667","longitude":"-81.69843056"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/02151500","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/02151500/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":"Previous Flowbands: \nRange of Boatable Flows (R0-R9): 800 - 2000 cfs  Comment: 600 to 800 cfs seems to be the baseline for natural flow at the Boiling Springs gauge, during the summer. \n\nMigration Errors: \nSingle range is valid but doesn't provide low/medium/high runnable\nThere is one comment for all of low/medium/high runnable.","comment":"Gauge is 45 miles or about 15 hrs below the run.","status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"341","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["109657","4sInAbzNaSruu5zacvvlW","N3ANoZWerWvxGjoattVjp","h1MnzUPtgR76NHDk8qZdC","114909"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-82.185019,35.333365],[-82.18471,35.333192],[-82.18444,35.333196],[-82.184189,35.333347],[-82.183967,35.333827],[-82.183753,35.334018],[-82.183375,35.335599],[-82.182782,35.336396],[-82.182547,35.336946],[-82.182488,35.337517],[-82.18258,35.337998],[-82.182566,35.338321],[-82.182431,35.339064],[-82.182324,35.339159],[-82.182292,35.339336],[-82.182052,35.339669],[-82.181817,35.340219],[-82.181369,35.340961],[-82.181127,35.341547],[-82.181115,35.341617],[-82.180433,35.342404],[-82.180299,35.342894],[-82.180015,35.343221],[-82.17999,35.343363],[-82.179813,35.343595],[-82.179378,35.344013],[-82.178988,35.344184],[-8